# Job Hunter AI — sources file (copy to sources.txt, point config.yaml's
# `sources_file:` at it). One source per line. Blank lines and #-comments
# ignored. Titles and locations are NOT here — they live in the `filters`
# block in config.yaml. These lines only say WHERE to look.
#
# This file is MERGED with config.yaml's inline `sources:` (appended, not
# synced) — you don't keep the two in step; a board in either place is scraped.
# Only read if config.yaml has a `sources_file:` line pointing here; without
# that pointer, this file is ignored no matter what it contains.
#
#   seek                 # a SEEK search, driven by filters
#   adzuna <country>     # an Adzuna search (au, in, ...); needs adzuna: creds
#   greenhouse <token>   # an ATS board, by company token
#   lever <token>
#   ashby <token>
#
# Or just paste the board's careers URL — the type + token are auto-detected:
#   https://boards.greenhouse.io/<token>      # → greenhouse <token>
#   https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/<token>  # newer Greenhouse host
#   https://jobs.lever.co/<token>             # → lever <token>
#   https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/<token>          # → ashby <token>

seek
adzuna au
adzuna in
greenhouse stripe
greenhouse airbnb
lever figma
lever ramp
ashby ashby

# Same boards, pasted as URLs instead (scheme optional, deep links fine):
# https://boards.greenhouse.io/stripe
# https://jobs.lever.co/metabase
# https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/ramp
